          <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight flex items-center gap-2 text-balance">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-6 bg-link rounded-full"></span>
            6. The 4 Most Dangerous Cron Traps
          </h2>
          <p>
            Cron syntax has several subtle corner cases that frequently cause severe production incidents. Here is what to watch out for:
          </p>

          <div class="space-y-5">
            
            <!-- Trap 1 -->
            <div class="bg-canvas-soft border-l-4 border-error p-5 rounded-r-xl space-y-2">
              <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white font-mono uppercase flex items-center gap-2">
                <span class="text-error">Trap 1:</span> The Minute Asterisk Disaster
              </h3>
              <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
                Writing <code class="text-error font-mono font-bold bg-canvas-soft-2 px-1 rounded">* 2 * * *</code> instead of <code class="text-link font-mono font-bold bg-canvas-soft-2 px-1 rounded">0 2 * * *</code>. The asterisk means <em>every minute</em>. As a result, your task executes 60 times between 2:00 AM and 2:59 AM instead of once! Always ensure you put <code class="text-white font-mono">0</code> in the minute slot when scheduling hourly or daily runs.
              </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Trap 2 -->
            <div class="bg-canvas-soft border-l-4 border-warning p-5 rounded-r-xl space-y-2">
              <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white font-mono uppercase flex items-center gap-2">
                <span class="text-warning">Trap 2:</span> The Day-of-Month vs Day-of-Week OR-Union
              </h3>
              <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
                In standard POSIX crontab, if you specify <strong>both</strong> Day of Month and Day of Week (neither is an asterisk), the cron daemon evaluates them as an <strong>OR condition</strong>, not an AND condition! For example, <code class="text-white font-mono">0 0 15 * 5</code> runs on the 15th of the month <em>AND</em> on every Friday! If you want "Friday the 15th only", you must enforce the check inside your script logic.
              </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Trap 3 -->
            <div class="bg-canvas-soft border-l-4 border-cyan-400 p-5 rounded-r-xl space-y-2">
              <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white font-mono uppercase flex items-center gap-2">
                <span class="text-cyan-400">Trap 3:</span> Server Timezones & Daylight Saving Time (DST)
              </h3>
              <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
                If your host server runs on local time with Daylight Saving Time (e.g. US Eastern or Central European Time), jobs scheduled at 2:30 AM will be <strong>skipped entirely</strong> when clocks spring forward one hour in spring, and <strong>executed twice</strong> when clocks fall back in autumn.
              </p>
              <p class="text-xs text-white font-mono">
                ✓ Best Practice: Always set production servers and container orchestrators to UTC (<code class="text-link font-mono">TZ=UTC</code>).
              </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Trap 4 -->
            <div class="bg-canvas-soft border-l-4 border-violet-400 p-5 rounded-r-xl space-y-2">
              <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-white font-mono uppercase flex items-center gap-2">
                <span class="text-violet-400">Trap 4:</span> Stripped Environment & PATH Variables
              </h3>
              <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
                When cron executes a command, it runs in a minimal, stripped shell environment. Binaries like <code class="text-white font-mono">node</code>, <code class="text-white font-mono">python3</code>, or <code class="text-white font-mono">aws</code> located in user folders (<code class="text-white font-mono">/usr/local/bin</code> or <code class="text-white font-mono">~/.nvm</code>) may not be in PATH, resulting in silent <code class="text-error font-mono">command not found</code> failures. Always specify full binary paths or source your profile in crontab.
              </p>
            </div>

          </div>
